1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,360
Brighten up the peace,
then try stepping away.

2
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,020
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,500
Someone who goes home right
after finishing their errands.

4
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,360
Wappara, whoa, wappara.

5
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:40,020
Wapparafuwachi wappara.

6
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:45,560
Don't feel sorry for me in this narrow town.

7
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:49,380
Where are you going?
If you're in a hurry, take the long way.

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:58,540
If, by any chance,
there's someone better than me,

9
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:03,020
tell me about it, tell me all night long.

10
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:12,820
I don't mind waiting.

11
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:17,020
Because I'm a woman of Kame-za.

12
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,680
I won't lose, woman of Ginza.

13
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:26,500
I'll love you for years and years.

14
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,880
The everyday life of a Kame-za woman.

15
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:42,100
At the time, the year was 1999 A.D.

16
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,640
the war that suddenly broke
out had seemed to be dragging on,

17
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,860
but afterward it rapidly
moved toward an end,

18
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:53,580
and then...

19
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,920
Wait!

20
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,600
Are you going to be
completely picked apart now?!

21
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:05,100
I'm going to turn this around from here!

22
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,920
Burn Tenso!

23
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:18,660
Looks like the match is decided.

24
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:19,280
No way!

25
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:26,266
Yes! After a fierce two-hour,
fifteen-minute battle,

26
00:02:26,316 --> 00:02:28,340
we've finally claimed victory!

27
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,680
Fight, Trump Upset!

28
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:36,540
Darn it!

29
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:38,400
Even if it's just playing cards,

30
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,440
to lose to Ryo-chan!

31
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:41,720
Well then,

32
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:45,780
the loser has to face a penalty game, right?

33
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:46,900
Penalty game

34
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,580
That voice...

35
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,360
Ryo-chan?

36
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:56,360
Ryo-chan!

37
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:12,440
War takes too long.
Shall we play something quicker next time?

38
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:14,740
Then how about Speed, straight up?

39
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:17,020
Speed? Bring it on.

40
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:21,500
Speed is a game that's all
about racing to be the fastest.

41
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:24,020
You slap down one card
at a time from your hand,

42
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:27,000
and keep building on those
cards regardless of suit.

43
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,660
Whoever runs out of cards first wins.

44
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:33,200
I've never lost a game of Speed, not once.

45
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,460
Fool.

46
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:37,880
You think you can beat me at Speed? Me?

47
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:44,140
So if it's 3 and 9, then it's 4 or 10.

48
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,220
Don't be so naive, Reiko!

49
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:50,880
Did you see that? The Thousand-Armed Kannon!

50
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:51,880
So fast!

51
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,240
What is this, Speed Rander?

52
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,140
This is...

53
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:57,800
At this speed, your hands look
like they have several arms, senpai.

54
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,500
Just like the Thousand-Armed Kannon!

55
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:09,840
Ataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataata!

56
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,540
Ryo-san wins by a landslide!

57
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:14,600
So Reiko couldn't play
a single card in the end?

58
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,980
The gap in skill is just too big.

59
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,281
Well, have you learned your lesson?

60
00:04:20,331 --> 00:04:24,220
Trying to beat me at Speed?
You're ten years too early.

61
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:26,380
Alright, let's go with the penalty game.

62
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:33,180
Here's another one.

63
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,400
Why don't we play something
everyone can join in on next?

64
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:41,540
Indian Poker?

65
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,462
You stick a card to your forehead like this,

66
00:04:44,512 --> 00:04:47,320
and the higher number wins.
A 13 is the strongest.

67
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:49,080
So you can't see your own card, right?

68
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:52,069
That's what makes it
different from regular poker.

69
00:04:52,119 --> 00:04:54,460
If you think your opponent's card is stronger,
you fold.

70
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:55,060
I see.

71
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,520
Match bet, five chips. Alright, here we go.

72
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:58,000
Yeah.

73
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:59,980
1, 2, 3!

74
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,160
Gah!

75
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:05,720
These guys have such good
luck with their draws.

76
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:08,120
Looks like we can't beat these two.

77
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:15,780
We can't possibly beat these two.
Alright, chips. First, five.

78
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,400
I'm folding too.

79
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:24,140
So that's what it was. Darn it, I shouldn't have folded.
Now the outcome is unclear.

80
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:32,020
Nakagawa, what are you going to do? Me? Are you folding,
or are you going head-to-head with me? Which is it?

81
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:38,540
Th-that's ten chips. What are you going to do, Nakagawa?
W-wait a second, please.

82
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,280
Senpai's card is a 3.

83
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:45,440
Logically speaking,
the chance that I lose is low.

84
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:47,380
But look at Senpai's confidence.

85
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,160
Could I be a 1 or a 2?

86
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,500
20 chips.

87
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:53,940
So you're going head-to-head, Nakagawa?

88
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:55,520
Don't regret it.

89
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,160
30 chips.

90
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,840
Going head-to-head is fine, but...

91
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:02,020
Don't you dare regret it later.

92
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:04,320
Head-to-head, Nakagawa!

93
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,580
I'm folding, I'm out.

94
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,380
I fold.

95
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,574
Whoo! Yes!

96
00:06:09,624 --> 00:06:11,420
I win!

97
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,520
With this hand I couldn't possibly lose!

98
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,600
Hey, that's cruel!

99
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:23,000
Ryo-chan's all bluff,
you should've just gone head-to-head!

100
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:23,920
Exactly.

101
00:06:24,518 --> 00:06:28,340
For a loser,
you've got a lot of nerve talking like that.

102
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:29,480
Hehe.

103
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:31,300
Dariganiaa!

104
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,000
Ugh, g-gh, I can't breathe.

105
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,680
Chichikuri mambo de, kyuu.

106
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:35,620
Don't look.

107
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:38,700
But can we skip the penalty game?

108
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:42,560
No way!
Then what's the fun in playing the game?

109
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:46,900
Oh, there is one.
A game that's fun even without a penalty.

110
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:50,084
The winner gets to sit in the finest chair,

111
00:06:50,134 --> 00:06:53,760
while the loser kneels on the ground.
The ultimate game.

112
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:54,920
Ultimate?

113
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:55,900
Game?

114
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,680
The name of that game is...

115
00:06:58,760 --> 00:06:59,940
Daifugo.

116
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:01,560
Daifugo?

117
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:02,620
I don't know.

118
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:03,840
What kind of game is it?

119
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,520
I brought it, Ryotsu!

120
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,340
Okuda Sakonji!

121
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:11,020
Senpai, what is this chair?

122
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:14,160
It's the Daifugo chair we use
when we play Daifugo at Ryo's.

123
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:16,580
Only the winner gets to sit in this chair.

124
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,220
So this is it.

125
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:21,180
I told you this is the Daifugo chair,
didn't I?

126
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,580
Don't touch this medal.

127
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,860
I absolutely cannot lose today's match.

128
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:26,920
Because

129
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:30,840
Dokimemo Cushion

130
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:35,040
Until now, I could never become the Daifugo.

131
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:38,280
But with this,
my determination to win surges.

132
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:41,360
I can't let anyone else
get close to this path.

133
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,820
Well then, that's it.

134
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:48,080
In Daifugo, each player plays a
card higher than the one before,

135
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:50,720
and the first to get rid
of all their cards wins.

136
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,440
3 is the weakest, and 2 is the strongest.

137
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:56,520
Also, if you have two or more cards of the same number,
you can play them all at once.

138
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,200
Well then, I'll go first.

139
00:07:58,720 --> 00:07:59,040
3

140
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:02,040
I've got a Jack and

141
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:05,240
Wait, from 4 up,
you discard starting with the lowest number.

142
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:08,080
No the Jack is the lowest one.

143
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:08,640
What?

144
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:09,280
Ace.

145
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,860
Hey, hey, Reiko, what's going on?

146
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:13,600
Because we only have face cards,
Aces, and Twos.

147
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:15,280
Me too.

148
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:19,120
So those two have all the strong cards?

149
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,780
We can't possibly win.

150
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:23,740
I'm not giving up.
Saori's chair is on the line.

151
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:25,480
Pair of Kings.

152
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,960
Pair of Aces.

153
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:28,080
Jack.

154
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:29,360
Queen.

155
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:30,380
Ace.

156
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:32,620
Pair of Jacks.

157
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,020
Pair of Queens.

158
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,200
Pair of Twos.

159
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:38,660
Pass

160
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:39,680
Pass

161
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,200
Pass

162
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:41,940
2

163
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,120
13

164
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,460
I'm number one.

165
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,220
2

166
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:47,480
12

167
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,500
I'm number two, then.

168
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,800
Racer Ollie

169
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:54,120
Then I'll go next.

170
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,220
3 and

171
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:55,820
4

172
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,540
5

173
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:59,800
This has turned into a pretty low-level fight,
hasn't it.

174
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:01,600
Pass

175
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:02,240
Pass

176
00:09:03,060 --> 00:09:03,800
I'm out!

177
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:07,160
Next time,
I'll definitely become Daifugo, Saori.

178
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:11,000
Damn it, I've got just one card left,
and I still can't get rid of it!

179
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Ryo-san, pass?

180
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,440
Just hurry up and play.

181
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:14,980
Are you sure? Really?

182
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:16,240
Stop being so dramatic about it.

183
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:17,480
Well, then.

184
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:18,980
3

185
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:21,160
Yes! I win!

186
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,220
Double...

187
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:23,460
Pass

188
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:24,840
Double sixes.

189
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:25,800
Pass.

190
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,040
Double eights.

191
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:28,240
Pass.

192
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:28,880
Last one!

193
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,700
Why don't you play them one card at a time?

194
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:35,760
It's not like we're breaking any rules.

195
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:38,740
I don't want to be a Daifugo either.

196
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:40,360
That's right, senior.

197
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,940
More importantly, Ryo-chan,
you remember, don't you?

198
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:44,940
What happens to the Daifugo?

199
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:49,580
Damn it,
I never thought I'd end up sitting here.

200
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:51,180
Terai-san gets no cushion,

201
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:53,000
Sakonji-san gets one cushion,

202
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,720
and I get three cushions.

203
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,400
And the top player, Kei-chan,

204
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:59,000
Well then, I'll take my seat.

205
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:02,280
W-what is it?

206
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:05,500
No, it's nothing.

207
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:08,940
Sitting there is the rightful privilege of the Daifugo,
after all.

208
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:10,460
R-right, of course.

209
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:11,120
Then...

210
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:13,580
W-what?

211
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,540
No, you can sit there.

212
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:16,720
Go ahead and sit.

213
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,280
Then...

214
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,200
Then let's just use it
as a backrest like this.

215
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,900
This should be fine, right?

216
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:25,800
Well, if Nakagawa wants to do it that way,
I suppose it can't be helped.

217
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,440
Then, excuse me...

218
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,900
Come on, the loser deals the cards.

219
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,400
Don't you dare, damn it.
I'm going to become Daifugo no matter what.

220
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:34,700
What's this?

221
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:38,540
Lucky! I got two 2s. This is my chance.

222
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,460
Ryo-san, it's time to exchange cards.

223
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,060
Right.

224
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:48,240
The last-place player has to hand the
Daifugo their two best cards from their hand.

225
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:51,900
Between second-to-last and third-to-last,
they exchange one card each in the same way.

226
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:54,760
So it's designed so that it's hard
to climb back up from the bottom

227
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,620
Yes, senpai.

228
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,420
Damn it, and I came all this way.

229
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,760
Oh no, I ended up with a terrible hand.

230
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,960
Then, Ryo-san,
the last-place player goes first.

231
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,380
Like hell it is.

232
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:12,260
Yeah, sorry, that's exactly right.

233
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:14,880
See, I knew it.

234
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:19,840
Damn it,
don't think this is going to end here.

235
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:35,100
Killer move! Five diamonds in a row!

236
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,860
I never thought you'd be
holding a hand like this.

237
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:41,240
Can we play this too, senpai?

238
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:44,980
Yeah, it's called a staircase. You can
play consecutive numbers of the same suit.

239
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:47,360
We always play with this rule at the dorm.

240
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:50,160
That's why there are
all sorts of local rules.

241
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:52,800
So don't complain that
the rules are different.

242
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,640
Looks like everyone's given up.

243
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:56,440
Alright, that's it.

244
00:11:58,420 --> 00:11:59,740
We did it, Saori!

245
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:04,100
But, Kei-chan, I've already gone out,
so I'm third place.

246
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:09,180
Ru! When will I ever get
to where you are?! Saori!

247
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:13,065
Damn it, I was just one card away!

248
00:12:13,115 --> 00:12:15,960
Don't tell me it's another
showdown between Terai and me.

249
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,040
Ryo-san, are you passing?

250
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,140
Yeah, it's you.

251
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,300
So we're allowed to play these, right?

252
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,060
Come on, let's settle this quickly.

253
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:22,860
Alright, I'm playing.

254
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:25,996
Dig... n-no way, this is where it's going...

255
00:12:26,046 --> 00:12:28,260
Wait, wait, wait, hold on a second!

256
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,140
You can play that? Ryo-san.

257
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:32,760
No, that's I pass.

258
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:34,280
Double!

259
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:38,300
Here it comes! Petty bourgeois pair attack!

260
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:39,340
Ryo-san, you're passing, right?

261
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,000
Pass.

262
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:41,980
Double sevens!

263
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,060
Pass.

264
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:43,780
Double nines!

265
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:44,980
Pass!

266
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:45,780
And a pair of threes!

267
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:46,320
I lost!

268
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:51,300
Ryo-chan, you're last again.
That seat really suits you.

269
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,432
Shut up! I had a 2 at the start too,
when I had a flush.

270
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:56,120
If only I'd had that, I would have won.

271
00:12:56,380 --> 00:13:00,200
That's just the whining of a loser.
I'd have dodged your first card too.

272
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,640
Saori!

273
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:05,080
The card exchange is exactly
why I can't climb back up.

274
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:08,180
Even so, that's the rule.

275
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:11,680
Cards keep dropping,
and the Daifugo will only oppose it more.

276
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,100
That's not how the rules work.

277
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:18,400
This is Japan! It should properly
be capitalist. This is unfair!

278
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,480
Capitalism, this game!

279
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,340
Those with power are the ones who win,
after all.

280
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:24,540
That's cheating!

281
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:27,340
Making the poor and the rich equal.

282
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,980
That's what a capitalist world is, isn't it?

283
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:32,580
Isn't that talking about socialism?

284
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:35,220
Seems like you've fundamentally
misunderstood something.

285
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:39,700
Damn it, you look down on us
thinking we're just poor folks!

286
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:42,540
No, Ryo-san, don't say that!

287
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:46,420
Honestly, a real millionaire being a Daifugo?
Is that even allowed?

288
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,700
That's exactly what it is, isn't it?

289
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,640
W-well, when you put it that way...

290
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:50,380
Right?

291
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:53,260
The real poor folks are the last and second-to-last place,
you know!

292
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,360
That's the reality of being poor!

293
00:13:57,620 --> 00:14:00,740
Don't you have any desire to climb up?

294
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:04,640
At least in this game,
don't you want to aim for the top?

295
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:08,040
But I don't want to end up
last by taking risky gambles.

296
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:09,140
You honest fool!

297
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:13,680
Climbing up by any means necessary is how a man should live,
isn't it?

298
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:16,140
Only you would do something like that,
Ryo-san.

299
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:17,660
By any means?

300
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,320
How careless of me.

301
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,720
These guys were all amateurs.

302
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,620
There was no need to play so refined a game.

303
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:36,240
This game's been a huge hit lately. If you use it,
it's the ultimate trick: stacking the face cards.

304
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:46,800
When gathering the cards, make sure the aces, twos and face cards end up on top.
When cutting, just pretend to cut while only the top part actually moves.

305
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:53,580
When dealing, subtly pull out
your own cards from the bottom.

306
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,520
Do it this way, and

307
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,700
Yes, that's perfect!

308
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,160
Yes, senpai.

309
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:09,140
Nakagawa, sure enough, passed me a 3.

310
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:10,280
It's from Ryo-chan.

311
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:14,760
Let me show you how I play Daifugo.

312
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:17,020
Here goes!

313
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,380
Three kings!

314
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:22,680
What's with this sudden card?

315
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:27,040
Well, are you playing or not?

316
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:27,780
Pass!

317
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:28,340
Pass!

318
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:28,980
Pass!

319
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:31,520
Well then, it's my turn again.

320
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,880
Four aces!

321
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:35,680
Ugh, ugh, ugh!

322
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:36,840
You look so cool!

323
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:39,060
A double of twos!

324
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:47,940
And finally,
the pair of 3s I got from Nakagawa.

325
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:54,260
Kei-chan, did you really trade?

326
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:57,520
Yes, I did get two 2s from you, senpai.

327
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:01,060
So you were telling Ryotsu
about all the good cards?

328
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,980
I can't believe something
like this is happening.

329
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:07,400
Then the Reversal Rule shall be applied.

330
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,700
Reversal Rule.

331
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:13,460
The Reversal Rule is when the player
in last place becomes the top player.

332
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:17,560
It's the terrifying rule where
all the rankings get reversed.

333
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:20,480
So I'm going to be out of the running.

334
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,960
Then I'll get one step closer to Saori.

335
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:27,140
Sakonji-san is right in the middle,
so her ranking won't change.

336
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:28,280
It's not like that, is it?

337
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,260
Something like that...

338
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:32,440
Even though I haven't
played a single card yet.

339
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:37,900
Haa...

340
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:43,440
What an unreasonable rule...

341
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:45,720
Unreasonable or not,
a rule is a rule, after all.

342
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:48,320
Well then, here goes... yokorasete...

343
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,780
Eeeeeeeh!

344
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,060
This feels really nice.

345
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:53,340
Saori!

346
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,720
Oh, hehehe.

347
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:59,600
The Daifugo's chair is so comfortable

348
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,280
Eeeeeeeh! Saori!

349
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,100
Ryotsu! What have you done, you bastard!

350
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,780
I can't forgive this, Saori!

351
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,620
Can't forgive it

352
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,520
Who do you think you're talking to?!

353
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:16,240
If you're that upset,
crawl your way up here yourself!

354
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,960
Until then, I'm keeping Saori, got it?!

355
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:24,160
S-sorry, Saori.
Please hang in there a little longer.

356
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,860
Well then, I'll deal the cards.

357
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:30,360
A job fitting for a Daifugo-type

358
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,260
Hold on a second!

359
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:35,540
W-what is it?

360
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:41,080
But dealing the cards is the job of the last-place player,
you know.

361
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:43,700
You just became Daifugo, so why?

362
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:46,120
You were just saying I'm
better suited for last place!

363
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:47,640
Silence!

364
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:50,380
Maro is not like you wretches.

365
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:52,840
I know the suffering of the poor, after all.

366
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:58,020
Even as Daifugo, I make sure to
do the unpleasant tasks myself.

367
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:01,080
Phew, that was close.

368
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,760
If you don't stack them properly, you could
plunge all the way down in one go, you know.

369
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,680
This is the hand befitting a Daifugo!

370
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,840
Senpai.

371
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:12,380
Yes?

372
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:16,260
Is this the best you could manage?

373
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,860
Just the cards you'd expect
from the last-place finisher.

374
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:20,620
Then I'll bestow these upon you.

375
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:24,920
The cards that came back are
better than the ones I handed over.

376
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:29,920
Maro is a compassionate man, after all.

377
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,260
But are you really sure about this?

378
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,860
Think nothing of it, think nothing of it.
Hurry up and begin!

379
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:35,000
Well then, here we go.

380
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:38,860
- It's a sequence all the way up to the ace!
- Hey!

381
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:42,640
- I can't believe it!
- I've never seen anything like this!

382
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:45,340
- Ryo-chan, it's a reversal!
- Hey, this is no joke!

383
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:49,340
Argh, something this
ridiculous can't be happening!

384
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:52,480
So that's it, Nakagawa,
you stacked the deck!

385
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:54,540
You're the one who dealt the cards, senpai!

386
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:55,931
What's stacking?

387
00:18:55,981 --> 00:18:59,020
It's rigging the cards
so you get the good ones!

388
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,260
Come to think of it,
Ryotsu's hand earlier was way too perfect!

389
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:04,300
Come to think of it, it was!

390
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:08,800
Besides, even though you're Daifugo, you won't give up the dealing job.
That's weird too.

391
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,560
Senpai, you don't mean...

392
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:14,880
Well then, little old me will
go back to the last-place seat...

393
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:17,060
Since little old me is the lowest-ranked,
I'll shuffle the cards.

394
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:19,100
Nakagawa-chan, you go over there, shoo shoo!

395
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:30,020
Come on, everyone's giving me such suspicious looks.
Little old me isn't cheating or anything!

396
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:32,880
Damn it, now I won't be able
to stack the deck ever again!

397
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:45,200
It's been a long time,
gentlemen of the precinct.

398
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:47,700
It's me, the super-rich Reiji Shiratori.

399
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:49,280
I've finally come to
visit after all this time.

400
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,380
Hey! Why doesn't anyone come out here?

401
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:55,020
And I've come all this way.

402
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,140
Pass, pass.

403
00:19:57,140 --> 00:19:59,140
Damn it, they're ignoring me!

404
00:19:59,660 --> 00:20:00,340
Look!

405
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:03,420
I finally make an appearance after all this time,
and you're still ignoring me?

406
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:03,960
Yes.

407
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,020
Seven double.

408
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,080
Another double?

409
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,860
Here, pick them up, you poor peasants!

410
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,960
Here, a double of elevens.

411
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,520
So you did have them.

412
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:18,140
Hey, look, it's the card you like, the card!

413
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:22,080
Shut up.
This is a crucial moment, so be quiet.

414
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:26,100
Hey, my sweet honey, how have you been?

415
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:27,860
Sorry for leaving you lonely.

416
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,840
How about a drive to Odaiba in my Porsche?

417
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:33,000
Sorry, but you're distracting me,
so go over there.

418
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:34,600
Tens!

419
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,940
Reiko-san,
why are you being so cold to me too?

420
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:40,360
Please, everyone, pay attention to me!

421
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,300
Pass, pass, pass.

422
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:45,940
Would you like to join us, Mr. Shiratori?

423
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:46,900
Daifugo.

424
00:20:47,060 --> 00:20:49,140
Daifugo, you say?

425
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,120
From the name alone,
it sounds like a game worthy of me.

426
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:56,160
No, you could say it was made just for me.

427
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:59,120
Very well. I'll gladly take part.

428
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:02,200
Since Shiratori's joined,
let's start over from the beginning.

429
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:03,340
That's not fair!

430
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:04,940
W-what is this!

431
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:07,220
There are two 2s in there!

432
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:09,640
A chance to become Daifugo right away!

433
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:12,920
Hey, Shiratori! You're a beginner,
so I'll let you lead first!

434
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,120
Hahahaha!

435
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,940
Fool! You'll regret those words soon enough!

436
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,220
Behold me!

437
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:20,060
Haaah!

438
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:22,560
Aaaaaah!

439
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:23,740
Heh heh heh!

440
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:26,540
This is the true power of a real Daifugo!

441
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:27,740
N-no way!

442
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,580
Two twos, just like that!

443
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,460
Well? Are you impressed?

444
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:32,780
Are you an idiot or something!

445
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:33,700
What did you say?!

446
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:35,920
What are you going to play after this?

447
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,340
W-what do you mean, what?

448
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:41,560
Damn, all I have left is garbage.

449
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:45,020
Pass.

450
00:21:45,020 --> 00:21:48,980
No, seriously,
the game won't work unless you play a card.

451
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:50,680
Fine, I guess.

452
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,720
There.

453
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:52,660
Here.

454
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:53,520
Here.

455
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:55,420
Here.

456
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,120
Here.

457
00:21:56,120 --> 00:21:56,580
Here.

458
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:58,660
Pass.

459
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:00,680
Here.

460
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:01,580
Here.

461
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:04,180
Pass

462
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:05,460
Yes

463
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:06,160
Yes

464
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:06,720
Yes

465
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:08,860
Pass

466
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:10,160
Yes

467
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:10,780
Yes

468
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:12,420
Pass

469
00:22:12,820 --> 00:22:13,180
Yes

470
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:13,960
Yes

471
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,580
Yes

472
00:22:14,580 --> 00:22:15,340
Pass

473
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:19,200
So Shiratori ends up last after all

474
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:20,820
Enjoy it while you can.

475
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:22,520
I'll be Daifugo soon enough.

476
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:25,260
Shiratori, last place,
you haven't forgotten something, have you?

477
00:22:25,260 --> 00:22:28,300
You've got to deal the cards to everyone,
you know.

478
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,900
I know, I know.

479
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:33,000
Lucky!

480
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:34,600
Four cards.

481
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,340
Here you go, Shiratori-san.

482
00:22:36,340 --> 00:22:36,780
Mm-hmm.

483
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:40,000
But I still have two cards, so I'm fine.

484
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:43,140
Hey, it's your turn. Hurry up and play.

485
00:22:43,140 --> 00:22:44,520
Hmph, just watch.

486
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:46,800
My cards, here they go, yah!

487
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,420
Hey.

488
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:50,660
Well, nobody can beat this card.

489
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:52,460
Th-true, nobody can beat it, but...

490
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:54,480
So, what are you going to play after this?

491
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:55,580
What do you mean, what?

492
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:57,180
Damn it!

493
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:59,620
Looks like this is going to
go the same way as before.

494
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:07,440
That makes Shiratori last 20 times in a row

495
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:10,180
It's not like I only had bad cards,
you know.

496
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:12,820
You only play high-numbered cards, so...

497
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:14,620
In short, you're just a show-off.

498
00:23:14,620 --> 00:23:16,520
I've never seen anyone this weak before.

499
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:19,280
From now on, I'll call you "Last-Place Kid."

500
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:21,220
Hey, Last-Place Shiratori.

501
00:23:21,220 --> 00:23:23,400
Hey, last place, last place,
Shiratori last place!

502
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:29,640
Says the guy who's poor in real life,
just like in the game!

503
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:34,220
Even if I'm last in the game,
in real life I'm a millionaire.

504
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:36,080
Me, pick up!

505
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:41,560
That was all until yesterday.

506
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:46,020
Just like in the game,
I've become a pauper in the real world too.

507
00:23:46,020 --> 00:23:47,420
You must be satisfied, right?

508
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,980
To think I actually went bankrupt.

509
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:52,480
Sorry, I didn't mean any harm,
last-place kid.

510
00:23:54,060 --> 00:23:56,760
I'm never playing Daifugo again,
you hear me?

511
00:24:10,940 --> 00:24:14,760
Amid the seasons that
gently pass before my eyes,

512
00:24:16,020 --> 00:24:19,580
I've gotten good at making forced smiles.

513
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:24,880
Left behind and changing, I am yours,

514
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:36,200
after our fights,
we always share a brief kiss.

515
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:40,280
You, with your teary eyes,
were so dear to me.

516
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:45,560
Such irreplaceable things,

517
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:50,980
how many of them does a
person ever get in a lifetime?

518
00:24:52,740 --> 00:24:57,300
You are me, and I am you,

519
00:24:58,500 --> 00:25:02,380
and that alone was enough to fulfill me.

520
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:08,520
Just seeing a dog laugh, look,

521
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:15,100
I felt like any pain I had was healed.

522
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,160
What the heck is this!

523
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:26,620
Is this the robot police officer that took
thirty years and five billion rejections to make?

524
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:31,140
Because, as usual, they never
revise a plan once it's been decided.

525
00:25:31,140 --> 00:25:33,040
And they go and build something like this.

526
00:25:33,580 --> 00:25:36,960
Next time, the robot police officer goes out on duty,
so look forward to it.

